{"nodes": [{"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__wahy_laya_finetuning_run4", "label": "Notebook: Run 4 - does the boundary pull the verdict down? (verdict-only vs boundary-only)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__wahy-laya-finetuning-run4.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fourth run on a rebuilt laya_v2 (equal passage split + v1 control folder). Hypothesis: boundary questions compete with the verdict inside the one shared model. Adds --questions flag (config records wahy_questions so eval and app ask only those) and boundary thresholds tuned on val (--tune-val). If both_verdict wins, the app asks the model only the verdict (3x fewer readings) and takes the boundary from the word-overlap rule. Same recipe as run 3 (2 epochs, batch 64, RLCD, max_len 2048, noul weight 3). Hub repos laya-wahy-r4-<run>. ~2 h."}, {"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__wahy_laya_finetuning_run4_both_verdict", "label": "Run 4 both_verdict (v2 passages+neighbours, verdict only)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__wahy-laya-finetuning-run4.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Result reported in run 5 notebook: AUC stayed low at 0.836, accuracy 83.3 percent, real rejected 12.3 percent, so removing the boundary did not rescue the verdict."}, {"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__wahy_laya_finetuning_run4_v1_verdict", "label": "Run 4 v1_verdict (old v1 envelope, verdict only) - the control", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__wahy-laya-finetuning-run4.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Result reported in runs 5-6: AUC 0.933, accuracy 91.4 percent, real rejected 4.1 percent - showing the v2 input format, not the boundary, caused the verdict drop."}, {"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__wahy_laya_finetuning_run4_boundary_only", "label": "Run 4 boundary_only (v2 + counterfactual rows, start/end cut-off only)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__wahy-laya-finetuning-run4.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Can Laya learn the boundary when it is its only job? Study model only: gives no verdict, must not be loaded in the app (app does not run two Laya models)."}, {"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__wahy_laya_finetuning_run4_both_noise_check", "label": "Run 4 both (= run 3 both on equal split, noise check)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__wahy-laya-finetuning-run4.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Re-trains run 3's both to measure how much numbers move between two identical runs."}, {"id": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__wahy_laya_finetuning_run4_boundary_competes_hypothesis", "label": "Hypothesis: boundary questions compete with the verdict in the shared model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__wahy-laya-finetuning-run4.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Evidence cited: run 2 more boundary items -> lower verdict AUC (0.945, 0.93, 0.918); run 3 doubled boundary items and the model with the most (both_synth) had the lowest verdict. Run 5 later showed the real culprit was the v2 envelope layout."}], "edges": [{"source": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__wahy_laya_finetuning_run4", "target": "notebooks_md_kaggle__finished__wahy_finetuning_laya_v2_run3", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "notebooks/md/kaggle__finished__wahy-laya-finetuning-run4.md", "source